+# Streak Freak
+
+A self-reported, gamified fitness tracker for gym, walking and running sessions, built with Expo and React Native. Early development: the app is still the default Expo screen, and the domain logic for activity logging and streaks is in place with tests.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Node.js 22 or newer
+- npm
+- Expo Go on an Android device, or an Android emulator
+
+## Setup
+
+```bash
+npm install
+npm start
+```
+
+Use `npm run android` to open an Android emulator, or scan the QR code in Expo Go.
+
+## Scripts
+
+| Command | What it does |
+| --- | --- |
+| `npm start` | Starts the Expo dev server |
+| `npm run typecheck` | Runs TypeScript with `tsc --noEmit` |
+| `npm test` | Runs the domain unit tests with Node's built-in test runner |
+
+## Project layout
+
+```
+App.tsx                  Entry screen (still the Expo template)
+index.ts                 Registers the root component
+src/domain/
+  dates.ts               Local calendar day keys (YYYY-MM-DD) and day arithmetic
+  activity.ts            Activity types and input validation
+  streak.ts              Streak calculation, derived only from activity dates
+  *.test.ts              Unit tests for the above
+docs/AUDIT.md            Phase 1 audit: current state, gaps, and the staged plan
+```
+
+## Design notes
+
+- Streaks are calculated from activity dates, not stored as counters. Several activities on one day count as one active day.
+- Dates are local-calendar day keys, so time-zone and daylight-saving changes do not shift a workout to a different day.
+- Domain code has no React or storage imports, so it can be tested without a device.
+
+## Status
+
+See `docs/AUDIT.md` for what works, what is missing, and the planned order of work. Not yet implemented: the activity UI, local persistence, the AWzm Coin economy, the meme reward system, reminders, and custom notification sounds.
+
+## License
+
+MIT. See `LICENSE`. The license file currently names Expo's copyright holder because it was carried over from the template; see `docs/AUDIT.md`.
