+# Streak Freak — Phase 1 Audit
+
+Date: 2026-10-27. Scope: repository state at commit `8d6b427` ("Initial commit"), plus the foundation work done in this pass.
+
+## 1. What currently works
+
+- The project installs from the lockfile with `npm ci` (Node 22, npm 10).
+- TypeScript typecheck passes with `strict: true`.
+- `index.ts` registers `App` as the root component, which is the standard Expo entry point.
+- The app config (`app.json`) is valid for Expo: name, slug, icons, Android adaptive icon.
+
+What I did **not** verify: the app has not been run in Expo Go, an emulator, or on a device in this environment. "Runs" is unconfirmed.
+
+## 2. What is incomplete or broken
+
+The repository is still the Expo template. Nothing in the brief is implemented:
+
+- `App.tsx` shows "Open up App.tsx to start working on your app!" and nothing else.
+- No activity logging, history, or deletion.
+- No streak, XP/AWzm Coin, or unlock logic (the brief's economy does not exist yet).
+- No meme, sound, image, or video library or playback.
+- No reminders or notifications.
+- No dark theme. `app.json` sets `"userInterfaceStyle": "light"`, which conflicts with the brief's dark design direction.
+- No `android.package` in `app.json`. Notification channels, EAS builds, and store listings need it, so it should be set before any native work.
+
+Repository hygiene:
+
+- `AGENTS.md` told contributors to put routes in `src/app/` using Expo Router. Expo Router is not installed. I've corrected that section (see §5).
+- `AGENTS.md` and the old workflow referenced `npx expo lint` and `npx expo-doctor`. No ESLint setup exists, so `expo lint` will not work. `expo-doctor` has not been run.
+- `.gitignore` ignores `/ios` but not `/android`. Continuous Native Generation creates both folders, so decide now whether to commit `android/` or ignore it. The brief is Android-first, so this matters.
+- `LICENSE` is the MIT text with the copyright line "650 Industries, Inc. (aka Expo)". That is Expo's template notice, not yours. I have not changed it: it's a legal choice, and you should decide whether the copyright line should name you.
+- No tests or lint existed before this pass.
+
+## 3. Dependencies installed
+
+From `package.json` and the lockfile (not upgraded):
+
+| Package | Version |
+| --- | --- |
+| expo | ~57.0.31 |
+| expo-status-bar | ~57.0.1 |
+| react | 19.2.3 |
+| react-native | 0.86.3 |
+| typescript (dev) | ~6.0.3 |
+| @types/react (dev) | ~19.2.2 |
+
+Not installed, and needed for later phases: local persistence (AsyncStorage or expo-sqlite), audio (expo-audio), video (expo-video), notifications (expo-notifications), and image handling. None of these have been chosen or version-checked yet. Each must be installed with `npx expo install <package>` so its version matches SDK 57, and its API should be checked against the Expo docs for that SDK rather than from memory.
+
+Also not present: `@react-native-async-storage/async-storage` (the brief refers to "existing AsyncStorage usage", but none exists), any navigation library, and any test runner.
+
+I tried adding `@types/node` for typing the tests. `npm install` with the sandbox's npm 10 changed unrelated lockfile entries (it downgraded `@types/node` from 26.6.5 to 22.20.5 and removed `libc` fields from native packages). I reverted that. The tests run under Node directly and the typecheck excludes them, so no dependency was added.
+
+## 4. Data consistency and storage
+
+- No persistence exists, so there are no records to be inconsistent yet.
+- Nothing has been migrated or deleted. There is no user data in the repo.
+- Design decision made in this pass: streaks and daily totals are derived from activity records, not stored as counters. This follows the brief and avoids drift on delete or edit.
+- Dates are stored as local-calendar day keys (`YYYY-MM-DD`). Timestamps are kept only for creation order.
+
+## 5. Changes made in this pass
+
+Files added or changed in the repo:
+
+- `src/domain/dates.ts`: local day keys, real-date validation, day arithmetic in UTC (DST-safe).
+- `src/domain/activity.ts`: activity types, input validation (type, whole-minute duration 1–1440, real date not in the future, notes ≤ 280 characters, all errors reported together).
+- `src/domain/streak.ts`: streak calculation. Same-day duplicates count once, yesterday keeps the streak alive until the day ends, a missed day breaks it, and the longest run is tracked.
+- `src/domain/streak.test.ts`, `src/domain/activity.test.ts`: 22 tests covering the streak rules, month/year/leap-day boundaries, validation failures, and deletion effects. They pass under `TZ=UTC`, `America/New_York`, `Asia/Kolkata`, and `Pacific/Auckland`.
+- `tsconfig.json`: enables `allowImportingTsExtensions` (needed for Node to run `.ts` imports directly) and excludes test files from the Expo typecheck.
+- `package.json`: adds `test` and `typecheck` scripts. No dependency changes.
+- `AGENTS.md`: replaces the Expo Router claim with an accurate note; corrects the command list.
+- `README.md`: setup, scripts, layout, and status.
+- `docs/AUDIT.md`: this file.
+
+`App.tsx`, `app.json`, `LICENSE`, and the lockfile are unchanged.
+
+## 6. Recommended architecture
+
+Keep it simple and layered:
+
+1. `src/domain/`: pure rules (validation, streaks, coin economy, unlock rules). No React, no storage, no clock. Already started.
+2. `src/storage/`: a thin repository around one persistence layer, with versioned records and a schema version number. Writes must be awaited, and the UI should update only after a write succeeds.
+3. `src/hooks/` or a small state store: loads records, exposes add/delete actions, and recomputes derived values from records.
+4. `src/ui/` (or `src/components/`, `src/screens/`): presentational components only.
+5. `src/content/`: the meme catalogue as one typed file plus an `assets/memes/` folder. Playback logic lives outside UI.
+6. `src/reminders/`: notification scheduling and channel management, separate from UI.
+
+Persistence should be `expo-sqlite` or AsyncStorage with a single versioned JSON document. For a few thousand activity records either works; choose SQLite if you expect queries across history, AsyncStorage if you want the smaller dependency.
+
+## 7. Staged plan
+
+Phase 2 (stabilise, next):
+1. Choose navigation (Expo Router or React Navigation) and set `android.package` and dark theme in `app.json`.
+2. Decide the `android/` folder policy and the license copyright line.
+3. Run the app in Expo Go and an Android emulator; record what works.
+4. Add a lint setup if you want `expo lint`, or remove it from AGENTS.md.
+
+Phase 3 (in order, each reviewable on its own):
+1. Persistent activity log: storage layer, add/list/delete screens, validation wired to the UI, restart test.
+2. Streak and daily totals on the home screen, derived from storage.
+3. AWzm Coins: a configurable earning table, a transaction ledger (earn and reverse on delete), and balance derived from the ledger.
+4. Meme content catalogue and unlock records.
+5. Post-activity reward: play only after a successful save, with a skip control and single-sound playback.
+6. Reminders with local notifications. Custom notification sounds need a native sound resource and a new channel per sound, and must be verified on an Android device before being claimed to work.
+7. UI polish and regression pass.
+
+Before Phase 3 item 3, I recommend agreeing on the coin economy (proposed in the next message) so the ledger rules are settled before code depends on them.
+
+## 8. Not yet tested on a device
+
+- Running the app in Expo Go or on Android.
+- Persistence across restarts (nothing persists yet).
+- Any audio, video, notification, or custom sound behaviour.
